# EASE — Bulk Repo Batch Execution

Two standalone prompts, one per surface. Paste each into its own agent session (Copilot Agent Mode / Claude Code) against the relevant repo. Do not run them in the same session — backend must land and be verified before frontend consumes it.

Shared facts both prompts assume (do not re-derive, do not re-litigate):
- Existing endpoints: `POST /api/v1/orchestrator/batches/run`, `GET /api/v1/orchestrator/batches/{batch_id}`, `GET /api/v1/orchestrator/batches/{batch_id}/items`
- Existing item shape: `{ repo_url, branch, cd_repo_url, cd_branch }`
- Existing batch request shape: `{ items[], playbook_name, goal, user_id, max_parallel, cd_mode, branch_strategy, enable_cd }`
- Existing item statuses: `pending | running | completed | failed | skipped`
- Existing execution path: Codemind → Tachyon (Gemini 2.5 Pro gateway)
- New execution path to add: Codemind → Devin API, as a second engine, not a replacement

